$DIR/test.p:6:23: invalid argument: length float64(1) (constant 1 of type float64) must be integer
    This error occurs when unsafe.Add is called with a length argument that is
    not of integer type. It also occurs if it is used in a package compiled for
    a language version before go1.17.
    (see "Package unsafe" in the Plutonium spec, section 20.1)
    (run "pluto explain E0133" for a longer explanation)
